{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent\/privacymanifests"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"article","metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"title":"Privacy Manifests"},"abstract":[{"text":"What each module can collect, the required-reason APIs it calls, and the privacy manifest it ships, so you can fill in your app’s own manifest and privacy labels.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PrivacyManifests","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Traffluent collects nothing on its own. It records only the events your app tracks and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"context your app turns on: every kind of automatic instrumentation and every standard enricher is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"opt in. It sends records only to the destinations your app gives a delivery, to endpoints your app"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"names. None of it is used for tracking as Apple defines it: no module links what it records with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other companies’ data, reads the advertising identifier, fingerprints the device, or works around"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the user’s consent or App Tracking Transparency. Every manifest declares "},{"code":"NSPrivacyTracking","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and lists no tracking domains."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each module that can produce data of one of Apple’s collected data types ships a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy"},{"text":" declaring it. SwiftPM and Bazel both put it in a resource bundle named","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Traffluent_<Module>.bundle"},{"text":", which Xcode and rules_apple copy into your app, where Xcode’s privacy","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"report finds it. A module your app doesn’t link adds nothing to the report.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Required-reason APIs","anchor":"Required-reason-APIs"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No Traffluent module calls an API on Apple’s list of required-reason APIs, so every manifest’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes"},{"type":"text","text":" is empty. The list’s categories are file timestamps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp"},{"type":"text","text":"), system boot time"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategorySystemBootTime"},{"type":"text","text":"), disk space"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryDiskSpace"},{"type":"text","text":"), active keyboards"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryActiveKeyboards"},{"type":"text","text":") and user defaults"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults"},{"type":"text","text":"). The modules that come nearest:"}]},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Module","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What it calls"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Why none is a required-reason API","type":"text"}